    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4354" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">attĭcisso</span></b> , āre,
			v. n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀττικίζω</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to imitate the
				Athenian manner of speaking</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc argumentum graecissat, tamen non
					atticissat, verum sicilicissitat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. prol. 12</span></i>
			; App. Flor. n. 18, p. 362, 12.</div>
